{
  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n* Pod logs for `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` report `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire ...)` alongside `idle_timeout=900s`.\n* Deployment `billing-api` sets `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900` in `demo-apps`, while `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` sets `spec.idleClientTimeout: 600` in `ack-system`.\n* Change CI-2452 configured `idleClientTimeout: 600` on `billing-db-proxy`, lowering the RDS Proxy timeout below the application pool recycling threshold.\n\n### Leads ruled out\n* Memory pressure and leak were ruled out because heap growth is a consequence of connection acquisition stalls during request retention, as documented in INC-2024-0312 and RB-014.\n* Load balancer keep-alive timeout mismatch was ruled out because errors originate from database connection resets by peer, not ingress timeout cuts.\n\n### Root cause\nThe RDS Proxy `idleClientTimeout` (600s) is shorter than `billing-api` connection pool recycling delay (900s), causing the proxy to drop idle connections prematurely.\n\n### Recommended action\nThe infrastructure team should update `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` in namespace `ack-system` by removing `idleClientTimeout` (reverting to default 1800s) or setting it above 900s.",
